<title>SOUTH KOREA: Ssangyong shrs soar on takeover rumours.</title>
<headline>Ssangyong shrs soar on takeover rumours.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of utility vehicle maker Ssangyong Motor Co rose by its limit of 450 won to 6,170 in early Thursday trading as rumours, denied by the companies, flared up again that the Samsung Group wanted to take over Ssangyong, brokers said.  </p>
<p>&quot;The rumours are not new at all, but are boosting the share prices again,&quot; said a Hyundai Securities analyst. Reuters he expected the vehicle maker's net loss to be cut to 150 billion won this year from a 228.5 billion loss in 1996.</p>
<p>But brokers said investors shrugged off the remarks.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727-5646</p>
